      "description": "A dark arcade room with three cabinets. The shutter goes up, the tubes strike, and the machines roll in. Insert a coin — a real 1 PAS transfer, signed by you and watched into a block — and the room scales until that cabinet screen fills your view. The games run in the page on emulators built into it: JEZNES on a NES (boingoing, MIT), Tobu Tobu Girl Deluxe and Geometrix on a Game Boy Color (Tangram Games, MIT + CC BY 4.0; AntonioND, GPL-3.0-or-later). Every cartridge carries an explicit licence permitting redistribution, shown on screen with its author and a link to its source. Frames are drawn through a phosphor tube: scanlines at the machine own line count, bloom, and no softening of a single pixel.",
